Q:
Find the following limit using forms: lim as x -> 1^- of (sqrt(x)+1)/(x-1)

A:
-infinity

Since x -> 1^-, x-1 -> 0^-. Form is 2/0^- which approaches -infinity.

Thus lim as x -> 1^- of (sqrt(x)+1)/(x-1) = -infinity

